# Notice

## Engine code

The project includes author-maintained engine implementations in both packages during migration:

- `src/dler_kun2/engines/` — the successor implementation used by the `dler-kun` console command.
- `src/dler_kun/engines/` — compatibility-era implementation retained until parity review is complete.

Both are distributed under the repository [MIT License](LICENSE), except where a file says otherwise.

## Vendored tool

- `src/dler_kun2/vendor/twimg/download_twitter_media.py` — legacy media downloader invoked through the Twimg adapter. It is retained with provenance; its aliases currently have no default CLI route because verified hosts resolve to the Fun800/mvfile backend.

## External tools

- **ffmpeg** — optional HLS muxing dependency for engines that need it. Install separately from [ffmpeg.org](https://ffmpeg.org).
- **Chrome or Edge** — optional runtime used by browser-dependent media resolution. The relevant adapter reports a dependency error when the browser runtime is unavailable.

Runtime Python dependencies and their licenses are declared in `pyproject.toml`.
